(853706, 94935, 13688, '<td valign="top">Ah yes...I knew he was an anole...but that didn''t have quite the alliteration I was looking for.  And I do admit it was taken a foot or two outside of "true" macro range, but those guys are like Van Damme and don''t seem to like it when you get the camera right up in their face<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-08-11 01:27:36.</i></td>', 'Ah yes...I knew he was an anole...but that didn''t have quite the alliteration I was looking for.  And I do admit it was taken a foot or two outside of "true" macro range, but those guys are like Van Damme and don''t seem to like it when you get the camera right up in their face', '2004-08-11 02:23:35.000000', '2004-08-11 02:27:36.000000', 0),
(853883, 94617, 2700, '<td valign="top">someone said it is out-of focus. it is. if you look under the neck, in the center of the photo- that is the focal point. seems to me that the eyes or area immediately around the eyes should be in focus. right now the image composition draws you to the focal point, the center. if you have no control of the focal point through the camera and wanted a nice frame, forget that. Put the eye in the middle of the photo and shoot. use photoshop to crop it how you like... this would have been a very very good photo. good luck</td>', 'someone said it is out-of focus. it is. if you look under the neck, in the center of the photo- that is the focal point. seems to me that the eyes or area immediately around the eyes should be in focus. right now the image composition draws you to the focal point, the center. if you have no control of the focal point through the camera and wanted a nice frame, forget that. Put the eye in the middle of the photo and shoot. use photoshop to crop it how you like... this would have been a very very good photo. good luck', '2004-08-11 03:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
