(1566272, 95339, 23394, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lhall:</b></div><hr/><i> See my comments on your "Cruzin''- revisited"; I feel the same way about this image.  I gave you a 7 on this, because I like the concept and the subject, and feel that it definitely has possibilities. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i copied your comments, as i''m dumping the revisited image ;-)<br/> <br/><b>lhall Canon EOS-20D  10/22/2004 05:25:58 AM</b> <br/>"I want a much closer crop on this. While I find the composition to be OK, I would really like to see the gray area cropped all the way up to the dark shadow of the wood or whatever it is the little guy is on, and also cropped in a good bit on the left side. The upper area has a nice, rich dark color that provides a good background, and I think getting rid of the gray would really make him "pop" out from the background."<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-27 05:44:56.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by lhall: See my comments on your "Cruzin''- revisited"; I feel the same way about this image.  I gave you a 7 on this, because I like the concept and the subject, and feel that it definitely has possibilities.   i copied your comments, as i''m dumping the revisited image ;-) lhall Canon EOS-20D  10/22/2004 05:25:58 AM "I want a much closer crop on this. While I find the composition to be OK, I would really like to see the gray area cropped all the way up to the dark shadow of the wood or whatever it is the little guy is on, and also cropped in a good bit on the left side. The upper area has a nice, rich dark color that provides a good background, and I think getting rid of the gray would really make him "pop" out from the background."', '2005-07-27 06:44:40.000000', '2005-07-27 06:44:56.000000', 0),
